{
  "name": "lock-time",
  "description": "closed-loop lock acquisition (#12): N in {4,16,64} x {cold-start (Vctrl clamp 0.9 V), worst-case re-lock (2.7 V)} at f_out = 80 MHz, band 5, Icp code 2, lock-detector window trim code 8. Batch-manifest port of sim/lock-time/testbench/run.sh (#828): same operating point, windows (cold = N us, relock = N/2 us, i.e. 80 / 40 reference periods), print step and 100 ps internal-timestep ceiling.",
  "claim": "spec/pll.md#lock-time -- closed-loop cold-start and worst-case re-lock acquisition against the design's own lock_detector, full 45-point PVT grid x N x condition (270 points).",
  "methodology": [
    "PORT, NOT A NEW MEASUREMENT. tb_lock_time_batch.sp is tb_lock_time.sp with the .control block replaced by manifest analyses and the .measure cards by raw_measures; the DUT instance, static configuration, clamp release, solver options and measurement expressions are unchanged. The per-(N, condition) values run.sh computes (reference frequency 80 MHz / N, window min(80 reference periods, 4 us * N/4) cold or 2 us * N/4 relock, t_force = 0.02 reference periods, divider codes from cloop_divider_params) are written out as the six points of the `np` axis.",
    "VERDICT. A row is PASS when LOCK is high at the end of the window (lock_at_end >= 1.5 V) and a last LOCK rising edge exists; t_lock_last_rise is optional because its failure to land is the FAIL condition the legacy campaign reports, not a broken deck. The DN-branch integration guard floor is 8.9e-4 V (3e-4 * 2.97 V), the legacy 3e-4 * VDD at the lowest supply; at 3.30 V and 3.63 V the legacy floor is 9.9e-4 V and 1.09e-3 V.",
    "WINDOW AND HOST. Every row's window is fixed by N and condition, never by SIM_WINCAP. Rows run on the batch fleet; the executing ngspice build is recorded per point."
  ],
  "dut": [
    "design/netlist/pll_top.spice"
  ],
  "netlist": "tb_lock_time_batch.sp",
  "nominal_supply_v": 3.3,
  "supply_tolerance": 0.1,
  "temperatures_c": [
    -40,
    27,
    125
  ],
  "corners": [
    "mos"
  ],
  "params": {
    "iunit": "8u",
    "b0_code": "1",
    "b1_code": "0",
    "b2_code": "1",
    "cpb0_code": "0",
    "cpb1_code": "1",
    "ldt0_code": "0",
    "ldt1_code": "0",
    "ldt2_code": "0",
    "ldt3_code": "1",
    "tstep": "2.5e-10",
    "tmax": "100e-12"
  },
  "options": [
    "rshunt=1e12",
    "itl4=200",
    "reltol=1e-3",
    "abstol=1e-9",
    "vntol=1e-4",
    "chgtol=1e-13"
  ],
  "analyses": [
    "save v(vctrl) v(lock) v(xdut.up) v(xdut.dn) v(xdut.vwin)",
    "tran {tstep} {tstop} 0 {tmax}"
  ],
  "raw_measures": {
    "t_lock_last_rise": {
      "analysis": "tran",
      "expr": "when v(lock)='vdd_val/2' rise=last",
      "optional": true
    },
    "lock_at_end": {
      "analysis": "tran",
      "expr": "find v(lock) at='tstop-1p'"
    },
    "vctrl_final": {
      "analysis": "tran",
      "expr": "find v(vctrl) at='tstop-1p'"
    },
    "dn_lvl": {
      "analysis": "tran",
      "expr": "avg v(xdut.dn) from='0.9*tstop' to='tstop-1p'"
    }
  },
  "topology_groups": {
    "lock": {
      "description": "closed-loop lock acquisition",
      "measures": [
        "t_lock_last_rise",
        "lock_at_end",
        "vctrl_final"
      ]
    },
    "integration": {
      "description": "PFD DN-branch integration guard",
      "measures": [
        "dn_lvl"
      ]
    }
  },
  "checks": {
    "lock_at_end": {
      "min": 1.5
    },
    "dn_lvl": {
      "min": 0.00089
    }
  },
  "sweeps": {
    "np": {
      "description": "N x start condition, with the per-point reference frequency, window and divider codes run.sh derived",
      "points": {
        "n4cold": {
          "params": {
            "sel0_code": "0",
            "sel1_code": "1",
            "sel2_code": "0",
            "sel3_code": "0",
            "sel4_code": "0",
